Provisioning a new machine is getting more complicated.
I need to update flake.nix and create its configuration directory, that's fine.
But I also need to:
- update any hostname-specific stuff in my chezmoi config;
- make sure I have ssh keypair access to it;
- make sure its root account has an ssh key that grants append-only access to borg@ancilla;
- make sure /backup/borg/passphrase is deployed as /root/borg-passphrase on it
  (or provision the borg key some other way?)

I'm halfway through the process of moving ancilla /var/lib from the SSDs to the ancilla pool. It's tricky because I need to mostly-migrate each service, shut it down, finish migrating it, replace it with a symlink, and bring it back up, and once I've done that with all of them move the entire mountpoint over, and I keep forgetting to do that when ancilla is freshly started up and it won't disrupt what I'm doing.



